pcm: gate the two reverb-injection switches on one mask test

The voice loop runs two `switch (slot2)` statements per slot, and only six of
the 32 slot positions -- 17, 18, 21, 22, 23 and 31 -- inject anything at all.
Both become one test against a constant mask, with the two bodies merged: the
second switch only touches pcm.rcsum, nothing between the two positions reads or
writes pcm.rcsum, and suml/sumr depend only on ram1[31][1] and ram1[31][3], so
merging them does not reorder anything observable.

Worth having on an in-order core for more than the instruction count: it turns
two indirect jumps per slot, 64 per tick, into two predictable not-taken
branches, which is not something a retired-instruction count shows.

Measured on the ROM-free voice-loop harness, all 32 voices keyed on:
29751 -> 29577 Ir per tick (-0.6%).

